horizon-husksync

This product is a Rust re-implementation of HuskSync
(https://github.com/WiIIiam278/HuskSync), Copyright (c) William278 <will27528@gmail.com> and
contributors (Copyright (c) contributors), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). It was written from a reading of HuskSync 4.1.0's
source (https://github.com/WiIIiam278/HuskSync, commit 827f7be): the snapshot JSON format, the data
type serializations, the MySQL/MariaDB schema and statements, the Redis keys, channels and message
format, the LOCKSTEP and DELAY synchronisation rules, the locked-player rules, the commands, the
en-gb message texts and the config keys and defaults. Changes: rewritten in Rust for the Horizon
game server; messages are plain text (no MiniMessage); no HuskSync source file is included. Database
statements and the SQL schema are reproduced from HuskSync's `MySqlDatabase.java` and
`mariadb_schema.sql`.

HuskSync's maintainers and contributors named in its about menu: William278, DaUltraMarine, CatTeaA,
HarvelsX, HookWoods, mfnalex, MrPippi, Preva1l, quiquelhappy, hanbings, Stampede2011, VinerDream,
WaterArchery, and its translators.

The item storage layout follows Item-NBT-API (https://github.com/tr7zw/Item-NBT-API,
MIT License, Copyright (c) tr7zw), which HuskSync uses; it was learned from that
library's published binary, and none of its code is included.

